    "result_text": "Dated grades are in, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec. After the last fix it passed 8 runs in a row.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V24__person_grade_dated.sql`, adds a `person_grade` table of grade + from-date per person. Existing grades are copied in with no from-date, so they apply from the beginning of time, and the old `person.grade` column is dropped.\n- **Saving a grade:** adding a person gives their grade no from-date. Editing records the grade from the form's date, or the sheet's today if the field is empty. It replaces only a grade recorded on that same date and keeps the rest.\n- **Rates:** each claim's due uses the grade in force on the claim's date. That applies to the rollup, period totals, settling, statements and the screen.\n- **Shown and audited grade:** the list and `PERSON_EDITED` both use the grade in force on the sheet's today. The list works this out in the browser, so it updates when today changes.\n- **Form:** a `person-form-grade-from` date field, filled in with the sheet's today. It only appears while editing, since a new person's first grade always applies from the beginning of time.\n\n**Decisions for you**\n- **When a person's due-total shows n/a.** The spec needs a person whose current grade has no rate (C) to still show `3.00` from older claims. So the rule is now: n/a only if neither today's grade nor any grade on a counted claim's date has a rate in force today, and no settled or stated claim keeps a figure. For anyone who has only ever had one grade, this is the same as before. I chose it to fit the spec; it's worth checking it's the rule you want.\n- **Import lines.** The app has no import feature, so nothing was changed for \"an import line gives its grade from the sheet's today\". Quick-add creates new people with grade A from the beginning of time, as it always has.\n\n**Two fixes to timing bugs that were already there.** Scenario 3 failed because of them:\n- **Settings form:** a second save made while the first was still in flight was dropped, and the first save's reply then wiped what had been typed since. Saves are now queued, and a field changed after a save was sent is kept when that save's reply arrives.\n- **Sheet loading:** the bar showed the sheet id before people and claims had arrived, so the test could act on a half-loaded screen and pick up the wrong claim. The id now appears only once people, claims and settings for that sheet have loaded. This is in `core/session.ts`, `session-bar.ts`, `people.ts` and `settings.ts`.",
